   558                              <1> 
   559                              <1> writeFAT:
   560                              <1> ;Given a cluster number to edit in eax and a number in ebx to store in 
   561                              <1> ; that FAT entry, this program will write ebx for cluster eax in the FAT.
   562                              <1> ;If the FAT is FAT 12, only the low 12 bits of eax and ebx will be used.
   563                              <1> ;If the FAT is FAT 16, only the low 16 bits of eax and ebx will be used.
   564                              <1> ;Input: esi = Cluster value, eax = Cluster to write at
   565 00000E14 53                  <1>     push rbx
   566 00000E15 51                  <1>     push rcx
   567 00000E16 52                  <1>     push rdx
   568 00000E17 56                  <1>     push rsi
   569 00000E18 57                  <1>     push rdi
